  (196, 'Changes to slice 2.3 after an independent security review, before it merged. Only full members of the workspace sign in: at the callback the web app asks Slack (`users.info`, with the bot token, `SLACK_BOT_TOKEN`) and refuses single- and multi-channel guests, deactivated accounts and bots, failing closed when Slack cannot say. Sign-out is refused unless the request comes from the app''s own pages (`Origin` or `Sec-Fetch-Site`). The session cookie is `__Host-` prefixed. Only a `T…` team id is accepted as the workspace. CI builds the web app (`pnpm build:web`)', 'The review found no way past sign-in, but guests carry the workspace''s team id in their token and would read every conversation the bot has had, including direct messages; 174 and 175 trust the workspace''s members, not its guests. The web app holding the bot token is the cost: both apps'' secrets are Production-only Vercel variables (39), and it is used for this one call', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-25T00:00:00Z', 'import', '196')
